    "text": "6 hours ago GREENSBORO, N.C. — Downtown Greensboro is about to come alive once again as the North Carolina Folk Festival returns for a three-day celebration of music, food, art, and community. Organizers say this year’s event is bigger than ever — and it’s not just about the performances. The festival is expected to pump $20 to $30 million into the local economy. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak 3",
